    },
    {
      "text": "This paper deals with the problem of inference in distributed systems where the probability model is",
      "bbox": [
        95.18417358398438,
        282.4830322265625,
        500.06060791015625,
        291.6087951660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "stored in a distributed fashion. Graphical models provide powerful tools for modeling this kind of problems. Inspired",
      "bbox": [
        46.4849967956543,
        294.9302978515625,
        500.0444030761719,
        304.0560607910156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "bytheboxparticleﬁlterwhichcombinesintervalanalysiswithparticleﬁlteringtosolvetemporalinferenceproblems,",
      "bbox": [
        46.4849967956543,
        307.38653564453125,
        499.97381591796875,
        316.5122985839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this paper introduces a belief propagation-like message-passing algorithm that uses bounded error methods to solve",
      "bbox": [
        46.4849967956543,
        319.8427734375,
        500.0771179199219,
        328.9685363769531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the inference problem deﬁned on an arbitrary graphical model. We show the theoretic derivation of the novel",
      "bbox": [
        46.4849967956543,
        332.2900390625,
        500.0084533691406,
        341.4158020019531
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithm and we test its performance on the problem of calibration in wireless sensor networks. That is the",
      "bbox": [
